  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "4 v 3 – play your way through",
  "description": "Four blue attackers start with the ball at the halfway line and try to play past three red defenders and score in the big goal with a keeper. Attack and defence go the same way. If red win the ball, they counter towards two small goals at the halfway line.\n\nSwitch players after 6–8 attacks and allow rest between goes. Too hard: play 4 v 2. Progression: let one attacker run out wide and cross. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Take up positions between the opponents, where you can get the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "If there is space in front of you – dribble and draw a defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Create 2 v 1 where the ball is."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you lose the ball – win it back before red reach the small goals."
    }
  ],
